<task id="020" project="messaging-communication-app-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>`MessagingChannelSender` + `MessagingArchiver` (ADR-045 seam impls; dispatch by `Message`; transcript → SPE)</title>
    <phase>W2 — Channel Provider (ADR-045 seams)</phase>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <estimated-hours>8</estimated-hours>
    <dependencies>006,007,010,011</dependencies>
    <blocks>051,070</blocks>
    <tags>bff-api, communication, acs</tags>
    <rigor-hint>FULL</rigor-hint>
    <rigor-reason>Adds the SECOND channel implementation behind the shipped ADR-045 sender/archiver seams — net-new `Sprk.Bff.Api` services (`MessagingChannelSender`, `MessagingArchiver`) + DI registration + `CommunicationType`-keyed dispatch wiring. BFF-touching (Services/Communication hot-path), calls ACS server-side, writes to SPE. Tags include bff-api/acs; modifies `.cs`; requires publish-size + CVE + code-review + adr-check per root §10.</rigor-reason>
    <parallel-group>W2</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>true</parallel-safe>
    <fr-refs>FR-01</fr-refs>
    <model-tier>sonnet</model-tier>
    <effort>high</effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>
    Implement the messaging channel provider as the SECOND set of implementations behind the ADR-045 channel seams that email-r4 shipped — proving the abstraction with a real second channel:

    • **`MessagingChannelSender`** — implements `ICommunicationChannelSender` with `SupportedType =&gt; CommunicationType.Message`. `SendAsync` transmits the message over ACS Chat **server-side** by calling the W1 ACS services (task 010 token minting + task 011 thread/membership ops), acting as the sending participant with that participant's server-minted chat token. It owns ALL ACS-specific wire concerns (resolve `communicationUserId`, obtain the sender's minted token, call `ChatThreadClient.SendMessage`, map ACS SDK errors to `SdapProblemException`) and MUST NOT leak `Azure.Communication.*` types across the seam. It returns a `ChannelSendResult` whose `ProviderMessageId` is the **ACS message id** — this is the value the inbound ingestor dedupes on for echo-dedup (FR-04, task 031/051).

    • **`MessagingArchiver`** — implements `ICommunicationArchiver` with `SupportedType =&gt; CommunicationType.Message`. `GenerateEml(...)` produces a **message-transcript artifact** (the `.eml` analog) as `EmlResult` bytes + filename; the pipeline writes it to SPE via `SpeFileStore` (ADR-007), exactly as `EmailArchiver` feeds `.eml` archival. Do NOT invent a new archive/storage path — reuse the same `ICommunicationArchiver` → SPE flow.

    Register both keyed to `CommunicationType.Message` in `CommunicationModule` (ADR-010, unconditional). Mirror `EmailChannelSender` / `EmailArchiver` exactly in shape. `CommunicationService` MUST remain Graph-free AND ACS-free — it dispatches through `CommunicationChannelDispatcher.ResolveSender(Message)` / `ResolveArchiver(Message)`; it must not gain any `Azure.Communication.*` reference. Do NOT modify the dispatcher, the engine, enrichment, the regarding model, or the review UI — adding this channel is purely additive registration (that is the seam's whole point / NFR-04).
  </prompt>

  <role>
    Spaarke BFF Communication architect. Authority on `src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Communication/`. Fluent in ADR-045 (channel seams — sender/archiver shipped R4), ADR-046 (ACS messaging channel — authored task 007), ADR-007 (SpeFileStore facade), ADR-010 (DI minimalism via `CommunicationModule`), ADR-032 (Null-Object), §11 Component Justification, and `.claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md`.
  </role>

  <goal>
    `MessagingChannelSender` (`ICommunicationChannelSender`, `SupportedType = Message`) transmits over ACS Chat server-side using the sender's minted token and returns the ACS message id as `ProviderMessageId`; `MessagingArchiver` (`ICommunicationArchiver`, `SupportedType = Message`) emits a message-transcript artifact archived to SPE via `SpeFileStore`. Both are registered keyed to `CommunicationType.Message` in `CommunicationModule`, unconditional. `CommunicationChannelDispatcher.ResolveSender(Message)` / `ResolveArchiver(Message)` resolve them with NO dispatch-site edit. `CommunicationService` stays Graph-free and ACS-free (dispatches only). Build clean; seam + dispatch tests pass; publish-size (vs ~45.30 MB) + CVE + bff-extensions Placement Justification + §11 Component Justification reported; `/conflict-check` before PR.
  </goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      **Mirror the email seam.** email-r4 task 016 hoisted send + `.eml` archival behind two `CommunicationType`-keyed seams: `ICommunicationChannelSender` (`EmailChannelSender` wraps the Graph send path) and `ICommunicationArchiver` (`EmailArchiver` wraps `.eml` generation), resolved by `CommunicationChannelDispatcher`. A new channel = register two impls keyed to a new `CommunicationType` — the dispatch site, engine, enrichment, regarding model, and review UI do NOT change. This task is that new channel: messaging over ACS Chat. Like email's `.eml`, an ACS chat message is a transport artifact the BFF processes into a `sprk_communication` (type=Message) record plus a transcript archive in SPE. **Dataverse is the record; ACS is transport.** (design §2, §3.1, §4.)

      **§11 Component Justification (NEW surface — the two impls).**
      • Existing: the seams (`ICommunicationChannelSender` / `ICommunicationArchiver`) already exist; there is NO messaging implementation of either — verified by grep (`grep -r "CommunicationType.Message" Services/Communication/Channels/` returns nothing before this task).
      • Extension: cannot be an extension of `EmailChannelSender`/`EmailArchiver` — those own Graph/`.eml` concerns and are keyed to `CommunicationType.Email`; a second channel is by construction a second keyed implementation, not a modification of the first (the dispatcher's `ToDictionary(s =&gt; s.SupportedType)` requires exactly one impl per type).
      • Cost-of-doing-nothing (concrete): without `MessagingChannelSender`, `CommunicationService.SendAsync` dispatching `CommunicationType.Message` throws `CHANNEL_NOT_SUPPORTED` (400) — no chat can be sent at all. Without `MessagingArchiver`, a sent message has no transcript archived to SPE — the `.eml`-analog artifact is absent, breaking the archive parity email has.

      Scope discipline: this is the messaging sender + archiver + their registration ONLY. Do NOT build the ingestor (task 021), the Event Grid capture (030/031), the thread resolver (040), or the outbound persist-on-send wiring (051 owns `CommunicationService` dispatch of the Message type + echo-dedup). Keep the impls thin over the W1 ACS services — do not re-implement ACS identity/thread/token logic here (that is 010/011).
    </background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Communication/Channels/EmailChannelSender.cs</file>
