    </relevant-files>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="FR-01">Implement `ICommunicationChannelSender` + `ICommunicationArchiver` for `CommunicationType.Message`, registered in the channel dispatcher; sending a message dispatches through `CommunicationChannelDispatcher.ResolveSender(Message)`; the archiver writes a message-transcript artifact to SPE.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-045">Messaging is a channel provider over the shipped sender/archiver seams — dispatch by `sprk_communicationtype`. The dispatcher, engine, enrichment, regarding model, and review UI MUST NOT change to add this channel (NFR-04). Adding a channel = additive keyed registration only.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-046">ACS is transport; Dataverse is the record. Follow ADR-046 (task 007) for the ACS-transport / Dataverse-record / BFF-mints-tokens posture.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-007">The message-transcript artifact is archived to SPE via the `SpeFileStore` facade only — no direct Graph/`GraphServiceClient` injection.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-010">Register both impls via `CommunicationModule` only, keyed to `CommunicationType.Message`, unconditional (ADR-032 Null-Object if any dependency is feature-gated). `ToDictionary(s =&gt; s.SupportedType)` in the dispatcher requires exactly one impl per type — do not duplicate the Message key.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-028">ACS transmit uses the sender's server-minted chat token via the W1 ACS services; MUST NOT `new` a credential / `ConfidentialClientApplication`; use the central `TokenCredential`. No ACS admin capability or token is exposed to any client.</constraint>
    <constraint source="NFR-02">Transcript archival and any enrichment side-effects MUST be best-effort and non-fatal — a transcript/archive failure MUST NOT fail the send. Mirror `EmailChannelSender`'s best-effort Internet-Message-Id capture pattern.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">ACS transport only for messaging; MUST NOT introduce a client-side ACS SDK; MUST NOT use Activities / OOB email / native Teams chat. `MessagingChannelSender` returns the ACS message id as `ProviderMessageId` so 031/051 can echo-dedup on it.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">`CommunicationService` MUST remain Graph-free AND ACS-free — no `Azure.Communication.*` reference leaks into it; it dispatches through the dispatcher only. Do NOT edit the dispatcher, engine, enrichment, or review UI.</constraint>
    <constraint source="root §10">bff-extensions Placement Justification in the PR (messaging sender/archiver live in the BFF — sole ACS-token-minting + `sprk_communication` mutation point); publish-size delta vs ~45.30 MB baseline; no new HIGH CVE. Run `/conflict-check` before PR (shared `Services/Communication/` hot-path).</constraint>
    <constraint source="§11">State each new impl's concrete cost-of-doing-nothing (CHANNEL_NOT_SUPPORTED 400 on send; missing SPE transcript) in the PR.</constraint>
  </constraints>

