        Implement `ICommunicationArchiver.GenerateEml(...)` returning `EmlResult` (bytes + filename); the pipeline archives to SPE. `MessagingArchiver` emits the chat-transcript equivalent — same seam, different artifact format.
      </pattern>
      <pattern name="Additive keyed registration" location="src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Infrastructure/DI/CommunicationModule.cs">
        Register the new sender + archiver as additional `ICommunicationChannelSender` / `ICommunicationArchiver` implementations; the dispatcher's `IEnumerable` ctor injection + `ToDictionary(SupportedType)` picks them up with no dispatch-site change.
      </pattern>
    </patterns>
  </knowledge>

  <steps>
    <step order="1">Read `EmailChannelSender.cs`, `EmailArchiver.cs`, `ICommunicationChannelSender.cs`, `ICommunicationArchiver.cs`, `CommunicationChannelDispatcher.cs`, and `CommunicationType.cs` to fix the exact seam shapes (`SupportedType`, `SendAsync`/`ChannelSendResult`, `GenerateEml`/`EmlResult`) to mirror. Confirm task 006 added `CommunicationType.Message = 100000004`.</step>
    <step order="2">Read the W1 ACS services (`Services/Communication/Acs/` — task 010 token minting + task 011 thread/membership/`SendMessage` ops) to identify the exact server-side API `MessagingChannelSender` calls. Read `.claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md` §F + §11 + the ADR-046 channel posture.</step>
    <step order="3">Implement `MessagingChannelSender : ICommunicationChannelSender` (`SupportedType =&gt; CommunicationType.Message`): resolve the sender's `communicationUserId` + minted chat token via the W1 services, call the ACS thread `SendMessage`, map ACS errors to `SdapProblemException` (a `CHANNEL_SEND_FAILED`-style code), and return `ChannelSendResult { ProviderMessageId = &lt;ACS message id&gt; }`. Keep it thin over W1 — no re-implementation of identity/thread/token logic.</step>
    <step order="4">Implement `MessagingArchiver : ICommunicationArchiver` (`SupportedType =&gt; CommunicationType.Message`): `GenerateEml(...)` produces the chat-transcript artifact (`EmlResult` bytes + a message-transcript filename). Keep archival best-effort/non-fatal (NFR-02). Confirm the artifact is written to SPE via the existing `ICommunicationArchiver` → `SpeFileStore` flow (do not add a new storage path).</step>
    <step order="5">Register both impls keyed to `CommunicationType.Message` in `CommunicationModule` (ADR-010, unconditional). Verify the dispatcher resolves them without any dispatch-site edit.</step>
    <step order="6">Grep-verify `CommunicationService`, `CommunicationChannelDispatcher`, the engine, enrichment, regarding model, and review UI are UNCHANGED (no `Azure.Communication.*` reference in `CommunicationService`); confirm dispatch of `CommunicationType.Message` now resolves the messaging impls instead of throwing `CHANNEL_NOT_SUPPORTED`.</step>
    <step order="7">Write tests: sending `CommunicationType.Message` routes through `MessagingChannelSender` (ACS `SendMessage` invoked; `ProviderMessageId` carries the ACS message id); archival routes through `MessagingArchiver` → SPE; the dispatcher resolves each by type; email dispatch is unaffected (regression). Prefer vertical-slice seam tests per ADR-038 (no `Mock&lt;HttpMessageHandler&gt;`, no DI-registration/ctor-null tests).</step>
    <step order="8">Run `dotnet build src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/` + `dotnet test tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/ --filter Communication`; confirm existing email send/archive tests still pass.</step>
    <step order="9.1">Run `dotnet publish -c Release src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/ -o c:/tmp/msg-020-publish/`; report compressed size + delta vs ~45.30 MB baseline. ACS BFF SDKs (`Azure.Communication.Chat` 1.4.0 / `Azure.Communication.Identity` 1.3.1) are thin over `Azure.Core`; expect a small delta. If ≥+5 MB single-task, justify; ≥55 MB architecture review; ≥60 MB HARD STOP.</step>
    <step order="9.2">Run `dotnet list package --vulnerable --include-transitive` — confirm no new HIGH-severity CVE (note any introduced by the ACS packages).</step>
    <step order="9.5">FULL-rigor quality gates: `code-review` on the diff; `adr-check` against `spec.md` (focus ADR-045 seam boundary + NFR-04 additive-registration + ADR-007 SPE archive + ADR-010/032 DI + §11 justification). Resolve Critical findings (path C) or surface an ADR conflict (root §6.5).</step>
    <step order="10">Run `/conflict-check` before the PR (shared `Services/Communication/` BFF hot-path — coordinate with email-r4 / notification-spine-r1).</step>
    <step order="11">Update `tasks/TASK-INDEX.md` (020 ✅) + `current-task.md`; record decisions (ACS send API used, transcript artifact format/filename, `ProviderMessageId` = ACS message id contract for 031/051 echo-dedup).</step>
  </steps>

