  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">`MessagingChannelSender : ICommunicationChannelSender` exists with `SupportedType =&gt; CommunicationType.Message`; `MessagingArchiver : ICommunicationArchiver` exists with `SupportedType =&gt; CommunicationType.Message`.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Sending a `CommunicationType.Message` communication resolves via `CommunicationChannelDispatcher.ResolveSender(Message)` and transmits over ACS Chat server-side (no `CHANNEL_NOT_SUPPORTED` throw for Message).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">`MessagingChannelSender.SendAsync` returns a `ChannelSendResult` whose `ProviderMessageId` is the ACS message id (the echo-dedup key for 031/051).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">`MessagingArchiver` produces a message-transcript `EmlResult` archived to SPE via `SpeFileStore`; a transcript/archive failure does NOT fail the send (NFR-02).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Both impls are registered via `CommunicationModule`, unconditional, keyed to `CommunicationType.Message`; no duplicate-key registration error at startup.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">`CommunicationService` contains no `Azure.Communication.*` (and no `Microsoft.Graph`) reference; the dispatcher, engine, enrichment, regarding model, and review UI are byte-unchanged by this task (grep/diff-verifiable).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">No client-side ACS SDK is introduced anywhere (server-side only).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">`dotnet build` clean; existing email send/archive tests pass; publish-size delta reported vs ~45.30 MB (≤60 MB); no new HIGH CVE.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>
    Depends on 006 (`CommunicationType.Message` enum), 007 (ADR-046 posture), 010 (ACS identity + token minting), 011 (ACS thread + `SendMessage`/membership). Blocks 051 (outbound persist-on-send wiring consumes this sender + the `ProviderMessageId` echo-dedup contract) and 070 (attachment materialization feeds this send/archive path). `parallel-safe: true` within W2 — distinct new files from 021 (the ingestor).

    Strict scope: messaging sender + archiver + their registration only. Do NOT implement the ingestor seam (021), Event Grid capture (030/031), thread resolver (040), or `CommunicationService` Message-dispatch/echo-dedup wiring (051). If a need seems to require editing `CommunicationService` or the dispatcher to add this channel, the seam is being used wrong — the whole point of ADR-045 is that a channel is additive registration (NFR-04). Keep the impls thin over the W1 ACS services.
  </notes>

